Dust engravings will need just one turn, semi-permanent engravings
will normally need a turn per letter but with an non-cursed athame
it will need just one turn for a full Elbereth. Burning with wands
(etc.) will also need just one turn for that word. If you plan to
engrave a word with more that 10 letters it will require more turns.

It's practically granted that dust engravings vanish when you start
melee (unless levitating), so it's just suitable to take a breath.
After some time dust engravings also erase if you haven't moved, so
don't count on it for longer periods, or inspect the engraving after
every turn if necessary.

What's the greatest problem in the first place is indeed that you
may fail to write it in the dust correctly. But you can always check
the engraving and usually it saves you more often than not.

